email.way_in.password_changed.body:
The password of your account in {workspace} was changed at {at}. Every other session was signed out.

If it was not you, use “Forgot your password?” on the sign-in page to choose a new one - that signs everybody else out - and tell your workspace's administrator.

{link}

email.way_in.password_reset.body:
A new password for your account in {workspace} was set at {at} through a reset link sent to this address. Every session was signed out.

If it was not you, somebody can read this mailbox: secure it first, then use “Forgot your password?” on the sign-in page again, and tell your workspace's administrator.

{link}

email.way_in.provider_connected.body:
{provider} was connected to your account in {workspace} at {at}. From now on you can sign in with it.

If it was not you, change your password under Your settings → Password and sign-in, choose “Sign out everywhere else” under Where you are signed in, and ask your workspace's administrator to remove the connection.

{link}

email.way_in.provider_disconnected.body:
{provider} was removed from {workspace} at {at}, and with it the connection to your account. You can no longer sign in with it there.

If it was your only way in, use “Forgot your password?” on the sign-in page, or ask your workspace's administrator.

{link}

email.way_in.passkey_added.body:
A passkey or security key was added to your account in {workspace} at {at}.

If it was not you, remove it under Your settings → Password and sign-in, change your password there, and choose “Sign out everywhere else” under Where you are signed in.

{link}

email.way_in.passkey_removed.body:
A passkey or security key was removed from your account in {workspace} at {at}. It no longer works there.

If it was not you, change your password under Your settings → Password and sign-in, choose “Sign out everywhere else” under Where you are signed in, and tell your workspace's administrator.

{link}

